    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# 🧪 Tag 4: Interaktion mit dem User\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Heute bauen wir Formulare, damit der User Daten eingeben kann.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 1. Das HTML Formular\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Wichtig: Das Attribut `name` im HTML-Input muss mit dem Schlüssel in `request.form` übereinstimmen.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# HTML Beispiel:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# <form method='POST'>\\n\",\n",
    "    \"#   <input type='text' name='username'>\\n\",\n",
    "    \"#   <button type='submit'>Senden</button>\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# </form>\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# In Python:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# username = request.form.get('username')\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 2. Validierung (Einfach)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Bevor wir Daten speichern, prüfen wir sie.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"def validate_post(title, content):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if not title or len(title) < 5:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        return False, \\\"Titel zu kurz\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    if not content:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        return False, \\\"Inhalt fehlt\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    return True, \\\"Ok\\\"\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## 3. Warum Blueprints?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Wenn deine `app.py` über 500 Zeilen lang wird, verlierst du den Überblick. Blueprints erlauben es dir, Routen in verschiedene Dateien zu packen (z.B. `admin.py`, `auth.py`, `main.py`).\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  }\n",
